msgctxt "[\"phpMyAdmin-5.2\",\"sv.po\",\"\",\"986\",\"ca45b8697171c6297d2a1d8a\"]"
msgid "It is usually sufficient to set {innodb_log_file_size} to 25% of the size of {innodb_buffer_pool_size}. A very big {innodb_log_file_size} slows down the recovery time after a database crash considerably. See also <a href=\"https://www.percona.com/blog/2006/07/03/choosing-proper-innodb_log_file_size/\">this Article</a>. You need to shutdown the server, remove the InnoDB log files, set the new value in my.cnf, start the server, then check the error logs if everything went fine. See also <a href=\"https://mysqldatabaseadministration.blogspot.com/2007/01/increase-innodblogfilesize-proper-way.html\">this blog entry</a>"
msgstr "Det räcker vanligtvis att ange {innodb_log_file_size} till 25 % av storleken på {innodb_buffer_pool_size}. En mycket stor {innodb_log_file_size} förlänger återställningstiden avsevärt efter en databaskrasch. Se även <a href=\"https://www.percona.com/blog/2006/07/03/choosing-proper-innodb_log_file_size/\">den här artikeln</a>. Stäng av servern, ta bort InnoDB-loggfilerna, ange det nya värdet i my.cnf, starta servern och kontrollera sedan felloggarna. Se även <a href=\"https://mysqldatabaseadministration.blogspot.com/2007/01/increase-innodblogfilesize-proper-way.html\">det här blogginlägget</a>."

